
-- ==========================================
-- QUESTION 1: CREATING A COMPLETE DATABASE BACKUP
-- ==========================================

-- Command to back up the sales database:
-- Run this command in the system terminal, not inside MySQL.

-- mysqldump -u root -p sales > sales_backup.sql

-- Explanation:
-- mysqldump exports the complete sales database.
-- -u root specifies the MySQL root username.
-- -p prompts for the database password.
-- > saves the backup into sales_backup.sql.

-- Regular backups are important because they protect
-- data against accidental deletion, system failures,
-- corruption, and unexpected changes.


-- ==========================================
-- QUESTION 2: BACKING UP ALL DATABASES
-- ==========================================

-- Command to back up every database:
-- Run this command in the system terminal.

-- mysqldump -u root -p --all-databases > all_databases_backup.sql

-- Explanation:
-- --all-databases exports all databases on the server.
-- -u root specifies the MySQL root username.
-- -p prompts for the database password.
-- > saves the backup into all_databases_backup.sql.

-- Backing up all databases before migration ensures
-- that important databases and their data can be
-- transferred and restored on the new server.
